The name and the logo

The GPL covers the code, not the name. "millerX" and the yellow M logo are not licensed with it.

- Unchanged copies may be passed on as millerX, with the logo.
- Distribution packages may keep the name when they only change what packaging needs (build
  flags, install paths, fixes for their system).
- A version with other changes to how millerX works or looks must carry another name and
  another logo, so nobody takes it for the original. Saying "based on millerX" is welcome.

As the GPL already asks: keep the copyright notices, and mark your changes as changes.
